                         Patch Metadata - Gen 1/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The seed used a simple "RY+RZ then linear-CZ-chain then RZ" block, which gives each block │
│                          │ only local single-qubit expressivity plus fixed CZ entanglers, forcing many               │
│                          │ blocks/uploads to build up entanglement structure while wasting parameters on redundant   │
│                          │ RZ pre/post layers around a fixed CZ line.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This candidate redesigns the per-block ansatz around three insights:                      │
│                          │ 1. **Parametrized entanglers instead of fixed CZ**: replacing fixed CZ gates with CRZ     │
│                          │ (controlled-phase) gates lets the entangling strength itself be learned per block, giving │
│                          │ the optimizer more direct control over how strongly qubits correlate — this is especially │
│                          │ useful since the feature map itself is IsingZZ (phase-type) coupling, so CRZ entanglers   │
│                          │ compose naturally with it in the same rotation generator family.                          │
│                          │ 2. **Ring connectivity instead of open chain**: connecting qubit 7 back to qubit 0 closes │
│                          │ the entangling graph into a ring, so information can flow both directions in a single     │
│                          │ block instead of just growing right-to-left across p=2 repeats and l=3 uploads. This      │
│                          │ should reduce the number of effective layers needed to reach full connectivity, improving │
│                          │ expressivity per parameter.                                                               │
│                          │ 3. **Full single-qubit rotation (RY then RZ) using shared parameters across dense/sparse  │
│                          │ layers to control parameter count**: Instead of independent pre- and post- RZ layers (as  │
│                          │ in the seed, doubling single qubit params), we use one RY + one RZ per qubit before       │
│                          │ entangling, and skip the redundant post-rotation layer since the next upload's feature    │
│                          │ map + next block's RY/RZ will already re-mix phases. This keeps parameter count close to  │
│                          │ the seed's while reallocating budget to the CRZ ring, which we found provides more        │
│                          │ effective entangling power than fixed CZ + redundant local phases.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Together these changes aim to raise validation/test accuracy and shrink the train-test    │
│                          │ gap by giving the circuit a more expressive, learnable entangling structure per block     │
│                          │ without growing depth or parameter count beyond the seed's budget, since CRZ gates on a   │
│                          │ full ring (8 gates) replace the CZ chain (7 gates) plus drop the second RZ layer (8       │
│                          │ params saved) — a near wash in gate count but a large net gain in entangling expressivity │
│                          │ per parameter.                                                                            │
