╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ry_cnotring_rx                                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the best-performing seed (RY+RZ pre-rotation, fixed CZ chain, RZ              │
│                          │ post-rotation; 146 params, 0.85 score), I keep the low-parameter fixed-entangler          │
│                          │ philosophy but improve connectivity and rotation-axis diversity. Key changes: (1) replace │
│                          │ the open CZ chain with a fixed CNOT ring (wraparound 0->1->...->7->0) for full-cycle      │
│                          │ connectivity without adding parameters, since CNOT mixes amplitudes more strongly than CZ │
│                          │ (phase-only) and the ring closes the loop missing in the seed's open chain; (2) use RX    │
│                          │ for the post-entangling layer instead of RZ, since the feature map (IsingZZ) and any      │
│                          │ Z-axis rotations already saturate Z-basis information — an X-axis rotation gives a        │
│                          │ genuinely different, less redundant basis for readout, especially since measurement is    │
│                          │ PauliZ (RX before measurement changes which Z-eigenstate populations you read out,        │
│                          │ increasing effective expressivity per parameter); (3) keep RY+RZ pre-rotation as before   │
│                          │ for full local expressivity before entangling. This keeps params_per_block at 24 (same    │
│                          │ count as best seed: 8 RY + 8 RZ + 8 RX, zero entangler params), same total N_PARAMS=146,  │
│                          │ but with richer connectivity (ring vs chain) and better use of measurement basis, aiming  │
│                          │ to raise test accuracy and reduce generalization gap further.                             │
