                        Patch Metadata - Gen 13/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ring_closure_reduced_params                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses CRZ+CRX alternating entanglers (8 extra params per block) which   │
│                          │ increased train accuracy but also generalization gap (0.10) versus the seed's CRZ+CZ      │
│                          │ variant (gap 0.08, better score 0.85). I replace half the parametrized CRX gates with     │
│                          │ fixed CZ gates to cut parameter count (reducing overfitting risk) while closing the       │
│                          │ entangling chain into a ring via CZ(7,0) as recommended. This keeps some trainable        │
│                          │ two-qubit expressivity (CRZ) but reduces the total parameter count per block from 8 to 4  │
│                          │ two-qubit params, and adds the ring-closing CZ at no parameter cost, which should improve │
│                          │ cross-chain correlations while lowering the train-test gap and improving parameter        │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
