│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Since only ANSATZ_SPEC is editable and the offset computation (block_index *              │
│                          │ N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK) is fixed, I cannot change the sharing granularity across repeats      │
│                          │ directly. However, I can achieve equivalent parameter tying by using a wire-parity based  │
│                          │ sharing scheme combined with fewer distinct parameter names, and more importantly, by     │
│                          │ ensuring params used in repeat 0 and repeat 1 of the same upload are structurally similar │
│                          │ but distinct only where needed. Since true cross-repeat sharing requires changing the     │
│                          │ offset formula (immutable code), the next best lever within the ansatz spec itself is to  │
│                          │ further reduce N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK by merging RZ pre/post into a single fully shared name  │
│                          │ set and reducing distinct RY groups from 4 to 2, cutting per-block params from 6 to 4.    │
│                          │ This continues the empirically successful trend (fewer, more shared parameters improved   │
│                          │ gap and accuracy from seed to current) while staying within the editable region.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Concretely: merge the 4 RY groups into 2 groups (wires 0,1,4,5 share one param; wires     │
│                          │ 2,3,6,7 share another), keeping RZ pre/post structure at 4 groups but merging pre and     │
│                          │ post into the same param keys (as already done in a middle candidate), and keep the       │
│                          │ 2-angle CRZ ring. This reduces N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK from 6 to 4, giving N_CIRCUIT_PARAMS =  │
│                          │ 4*6=24, total N_PARAMS=26, a large reduction from 86, testing whether even stronger tying │
│                          │ keeps or improves accuracy while shrinking the generalization gap further.                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.1504                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 0.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 0; deleted: 0; modified: 20;                                                       │
