│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_ring_shared_pretation_upgrade                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current ANSATZ_SPEC (single nearest-neighbor CRZ ring + CZ gates) underperforms the   │
│                          │ previously best-scoring "dual-ring shared" variant (score 0.91) that added a              │
│                          │ next-nearest-neighbor (distance-2) CRZ ring with only 2 extra shared parameters, plus     │
│                          │ finer-grained 4-way parameter sharing on the RY/RZ pre/post rotation layers instead of    │
│                          │ 2-way (lo/hi) sharing. Replacing the current weaker ansatz with this proven dual-ring     │
│                          │ structure should recover the higher validation/test accuracy, lower loss, and smaller     │
│                          │ generalization gap observed previously, while keeping parameter count moderate (98 total  │
│                          │ params vs 80 currently, still well within budget). This directly incorporates the         │
│                          │ best-known ansatz architecture from prior evolution history back into the current         │
│                          │ program, since the present candidate regressed to a weaker single-ring design.            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
